questions.stem:
A scatterplot shows Push-ups ($P$) vs Sit-ups ($S$) for 10 students.

\begin{array}{c|cccccccccc} S & 5 & 10 & 15 & 20 & 25 & 30 & 35 & 40 & 45 & 50 \\ \hline P & 15 & 25 & 25 & 25 & 35 & 50 & 45 & 50 & 50 & 60 \end{array}

Calculate the correlation coefficient correct to 2 decimal places and comment on the strength and direction.

The push-ups ($P$) vs sit-ups ($S$) data is shown below.

\begin{array}{c|cccccccccc} S & 5 & 10 & 15 & 20 & 25 & 30 & 35 & 40 & 45 & 50 \\ \hline P & 15 & 25 & 25 & 25 & 35 & 50 & 45 & 50 & 50 & 60 \end{array}

Determine the equation of the least-squares regression line, expressing $P$ in terms of $S$.

